From 3abca11cae618480250fdc24aeb1c360df41457f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 12:27:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(workflow): kernel is the source of truth for stage
 state; plan --issue links (B1+B4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

B1 — make `ship` reachable from a pure-CLI plan->dev->validate->ship flow.
Previously plan/dev/validate were stateless (STATELESS_ENTRY_STAGES) and never
wrote the `.forge-state.json` that ship's enforcement demanded, so any non-Claude
agent hit an unreachable wall at ship ("requires authoritative workflow state").

enforceStageEntry now, at the single stage chokepoint:
- WRITE (reliable): records stage entry into the kernel (`stage_runs` via
  driver.recordStageRun) for the active issue, resolved from the worktree
  branch->issue linkage or a UUID-encoded branch name. Best-effort but never
  silent — a failed write warns to stderr.
- READ (tolerant): when no inline/file state exists, synthesizes authoritative
  workflow state from the kernel's recorded current stage (getCurrentStage),
  which is what makes ship reachable with no .forge-state.json. Synthesis uses
  the full-ladder `critical` path (superset) so no canonical stage is rejected.
- `.forge-state.json` remains an OPTIONAL cache; the kernel is the authority.
- Fail-closed preserved: ship still hard-blocks when the kernel has nothing
  durable recorded.

The real CLI opts in via autoResolveKernel:true at both bin/forge.js call sites;
with neither a driver nor the flag, the kernel path is inert (legacy behavior),
so existing enforce-stage unit tests are unchanged.

B4 — `forge plan --issue <id>` links the EXISTING issue (claim-first flow)
instead of creating a duplicate issue + forking a second branch. Verifies the
issue via `issue show`, reuses the current feature branch, warns on collision.
`dev` is already bd-free (no bd call sites; the missing-Beads hard-stop was the
health gate, already advisory-only for the kernel backend) — locked with a
regression test.

Repro (fixed): a non-Claude agent running plan->dev->validate all green then
`ship` no longer dead-ends; ship reads stage from the kernel and proceeds.

Tests: test/workflow/enforce-stage-kernel.test.js (7),
test/commands/plan-link-issue.test.js (3). All affected suites green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
